tyle=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">50</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4+</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">AP 6, Autofire, High Recoil</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Tactical Laser</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">300/600/1200</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">AP 8, Energy</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Heavy Laser</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">500/1000/2000</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">M</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">AP 10, Energy</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Light Coilgun</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">300/600/1200</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">60</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">AP 2,Autofire, Energy, High Recoil</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Heavy Coilgun*</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">400/800/1600</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">80</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">M</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">AP 4, Autofire, Energy, High Recoil</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Light Autocannon*</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">600/1,200/2,400</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">400</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">M</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">AP 8, Autofire, High Recoil</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">High-Speed<br /> Autocannon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">800/1,600/3,200</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">300</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">M</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Autofire, High Recoil</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Heavy Autocannon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">500/1,000/2,000...</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">200</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">-7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">***</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">AP 17, Autofire High Recoil</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>.<br /> *:</b> Weapon is only capable of Autofire (including short, medium and long bursts)<br /> <b>+:</b> Increase the strength requirement when using Autofire (Short Burst +1, Medium Burst +2, Long burst +3)<br /> <b>M:</b> Weapon can only be fired accurately when mounted to a vehicle of at least Size 18. Any attempts to fire from a smaller vehicle incur a -1 penalty for each point of size less than 18.<br /> <b>Energy:</b> Requires the Battery Upgrade to use. Each point of Energy expended reloads the weapons capacity.<br /> <b>High Recoil:</b> This weapon suffers from high recoil. If not properly braced and set to handle the recoil, the shooter takes 1 bashing damage and suffers the Knockdown effect. Mechs with Strength equal or greater than [weapons size + strength rating] do not suffer the effect of high recoil.<br /> <b>Impaled:</b> If the target suffers 3 of more points of damage they take the \u201cImpaled\u201d tilt.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Impaled (Personal, Mech)</b><br /> A weapon or other implement has been driven through and lodged within your body.<br /> <b>Effect: </b>You suffer a\u20132 penalty on all actions due to pain and physical interference. This penalty continues until the impaling object is removed. If the object is tied to a tether you can only move up to the length of the tether from where it is anchored.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> Removing the impaling object without tools requires a Strength + Stamina roll with a -3 modifier. If successful, you take one point of lethal damage as you pull out the offending object. If done surgically or with tools, a Strength + Crafts roll is required instead, suffering only a -2 penalty, with no additional damage done if successful.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While I am posting material, below are some Vehicular Conditions. These are not Mech-specific, but they should be usable for most vehicles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Mech Conditions</b><br /> <br /> <b>Breakdown (Persistent)</b><br /> Something in the vehicles engine has malfunctioned. While the vehicle may be structurally sound, the defect prevents it from being started. A vehicle with this condition cannot be driven (regardless of its actual amount of structure damage), and must repaired.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> When the vehicles non-functional state causes the character a significant social or financial hardship.<br /> <br /> <b>Cosmetic Damage</b><br /> Looks matter, and this vehicle looks like hell. Dents, scratched paint, cracked windows and torn upholstery reduce the value of the vehicle (regardless of actual performance). The vehicle Availability rating is considered one less for the purposes of buy, selling, or trading. The shabby appearance of the vehicle might also impose penalties on some social rolls (never more than -1 or having to open an additional door).<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> <b>Death Trap </b><br /> The vehicle has suffered significant damage, and is actively hazardous to drive. The Drive suffers a -2 die penalty to Drive rolls while driving this vehicle. Any failed drive roll becomes a dramatic failure.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> The vehicle is taken damage within its last 3 boxes of structure.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>n/a<br /> <br /> <b>Fluid Leak</b><br /> The vehicle is hemorrhaging fluid vital to its function (such as oil, coolant, or steering fluid).<br /> The vehicle leaves a puddle whenever it goes and if the fluids run out it can cause significant damage. The driver may resolve this condition to gain a beat. Doings so causes the vehicle to gain the \u201cBreakdown\u201d condition.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>As described above or by repairing the vehicle<br /> <b>Beat: </b>When resolved to gain the Breakdown condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Lights Out</b><br /> The headlamps of the vehicle cease to function, either due to the bulbs burning out or by deeper electrical problems. While this is of little concern during the day, at night the driver suffers penalties to vision based rolls (ranging from -1 for early evening to -5 for pitch black starless nights).<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> structure damage to the vehicle, electrical malfunction<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>n/a<br /> <br /> <b>Out of Tune </b><br /> The vehicle is long overdue for a tune up. Worn sparkplugs and dirty air-filters impact performance across the board. The driver of the vehicle suffers a -1 penalty to Drive rolls and a -3 penalty to the vehicles acceleration. A vehicle that is this far out of tune can cause of aggravate other mechanical problems.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>n/a<br /> <br /> <b>Poor Fuel Efficiency (Persistent)</b><br /> The vehicle uses fuel at an increased rate. This could represent everything from a fuel leak to simple bad design. A vehicle with this condition consumes its fuel at a 30% higher rate, and often runs empty at the worst times.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>the vehicle runs empty at an inconvenient time or during a dangerous situation.<br /> <br /> <b>Tuned Up</b><br /> The vehicle has been freshly tuned, restoring performance to showroom quality. When engaged in high performance driving, the driver may resolve this condition gains a +1 die bonus to drive rolls and a +3 bonus to acceleration for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Exceptional success on a vehicle repair roll.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>As described above<br /> <b>Beat: </b>n/a<br /> <br /> <b>Uncomfortable</b><br /> The inside of the vehicle has a nagging flaw that makes prolonged trips a chore. Cramped space, broken air conditioning, damaged seats and other irritants can distract the driver at crucial moments. While driving the vehicle the driver suffers \u20132 die penalty to all rolls involving perception or concentration<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>n/a<br /> <br /> <b>Warped Alignment (Persistent)</b><br /> The frame of the vehicle is bent to a degree that make it pull noticeable in one direction or shake violently when accelerated beyond a certain point. A vehicle with this condition reduces its safe speed by 10mph.Anyone driving a vehicle with this condition suffers a -2 die penalty to Drive rolls when driving faster than the vehicles modified safe speed.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Accidents or Vehicle combat<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Getting into an accident while driving the vehicle with this condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Weak Battery </b><b>(Persistent) </b><br /> The vehicles battery goes dead easily and often. Even multiple changes of battery do not resolve the problem. Whenever starting the vehicle, roll wits + drive. If the roll successful, the vehicle starts normally; otherwise it refuses to turn over until the vehicle receives a jump start. Certain condition (such as cold or hot weather) and modify the die pool.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Repairing the vehicle.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>The battery dies at a dramatically inconvenient time.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 08-05-2015, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T17:04:30-07:00","id":616894,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the donation. Admittedly, I get hung up on specific mechanics. So, I am glad to have an assistant such as you to provide details and specifics over the ideas I try to brew up.<br /> <br /> As for what theaters of combat Mechs are supposed to be exposed to, perhaps it's a question of loadouts and scenarios as well as acquisition problems.<br /> <br /> You typically don't bring rocket launchers against even a horde of werewolves because even with autoloaders, reloading is too slow. You'll want a machine gun or heavier based on what you're firing. Or maybe an anti material rifle or coil gun to take advantage of silver bullets, since not many people can afford silver tipped machinegun ammo. Most cases, a generic SAW is what you're really fielding and that's fine for the most part. Also, sure you're really difficult to kill even in a Mech, but well, you're a big target.<br /> <br /> Question, is it intentional only superheavy mechs can take Size M weapons? I adjusted the sizes as per your recommendation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T17:15:17-07:00","id":616902,"title":"","content":"RE: Heavy Weapons<br /> <br /> It is intentional, but flexible. When I was going over Armory to determine what was the appropriate size of Mech for the most powerful weapons, I noticed that the example vehicles were larger [IFC -Size 18, APC - Size 19, Main Battle Tank - Size 20, Ground Attack Fighter -Size 22, Air Superiority Fighter - Size 20].<br /> The power and resultant recoil of these devices is so intense, I figured a bipedal machine would have to be very large and stable to not be knocked over each time if fired. I figured Size 18 was something workable that wouldn't damage suspension of disbelief too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T17:38:40-07:00","id":616950,"title":"","content":"Big props to you guys for the stuff you've been doing to expand on these. Should I ever find myself finally running the infinite macabre game I've always wanted to run, I'll make use of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T18:41:59-07:00","id":617009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=616950#post616950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big props to you guys for the stuff you've been doing to expand on these. Should I ever find myself finally running the infinite macabre game I've always wanted to run, I'll make use of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which reminds me, I should one day work on developing fixed versions of the spaceship rules. Preferably one that seperates fighters from frigates and above. Those rules have not aged as well as I'd like and I felt that customization needs to be corrected.<br /> <br /> In any event:<br /> <br /> <b>Disembodied Pilots:</b><br /> <br /> Not all walker pilots are creatures of flesh and blood.. or even in exist in what we would call &quot;realspace&quot;. Whether they be slackled ghosts, possessing spirits, or bound AI's, some pilots don't use Mechs to improve their physical abilities, rather they use them to have physical abilities at all.<br /> <br /> For the most part Unbodied Pilots are treated as normal Pilots when operating a Mech, whether be by possessing it directly, the Mech being suited as a vessel for them, or simply Storyteller fiat. However, there are a few exception. Due to lacking a body all together, unbodied pilots take no damage as a result of combat or collisions upon the Mech itself. &quot;Ghost Pilots&quot; use Power in place of Dexterity for firearms attacks, and the lower of Finesse and Resilience in place of Dexterity or Wits for calculating Defense<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:16:10-07:00","id":618500,"title":"","content":"So, I just realized something. Heavy Mechs, the only Mechs that can take Strength M weapons with no penalty don't have the ability to recharge Energy based Strength M weapons going by the RAW. In fact, they can't even take Energy weapons at all because of no battery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:42:51-07:00","id":618971,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Batteries Not Included? </b><br /> <br /> I might have to revise some of the text in the Upgrade Merits. You are able to purchase Upgrades <i>beyond what is included with the Mech</i>, but I don't think I made that explicit. This was set up so a player would have to put in a little more and pay a bit of a premium for that degree of power, because they are essentially driving around in a tank at that point.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, we could just include the Battery Upgrade as part of the base package for Light and Heavy Mechs (to go with the leather seats and sweet sound system).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T11:26:54-07:00","id":619189,"title":"","content":"I think having default internal power supplies works good. We can probably tie them to activity expenses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:41:46-07:00","id":620948,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Batteries Included!</b><br /> <br /> While the exact amount might fluctuate depending on the Tech level of the setting, I think giving Battery \u25cf to all the Mechs [which can be increased with Upgrades] would both the expand a Mechs capabilities and tighten up the overall mechanics, but not so much to disturb the game balance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:27:41-07:00","id":621405,"title":"","content":"You might want to change or provide an alternative to Battery then. Maybe Reactor? Maybe fuse them together?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:26:22-07:00","id":621445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZPoK1ANL6rU\" data-code=\"ZPoK1ANL6rU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZPoK1ANL6rU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> this may be relevent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T13:29:23-07:00","id":621586,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Real Mecha</b><br /> <br /> Well, Hell. We are living in the future now, aren't we?<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Updates</b><br /> <br /> I replaced the Battery Upgrade with &quot;Generator&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Generator (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </b><br /> The Mech has a self-sustaining power source, greatly increasing its energy capacity. Each point of the Generator Upgrade increases the Mech's maximum Power pool by 1 (to a Maximum pool of 5). In addition, this upgrade increases the rate at which Power is recovered to 1 point every 30 minutes. </div> </div> </div>In the main stats for the baseline Mechs, we would want to establish what the base recovery time is for Power ( I am thinking 1 power/Hour would be fair). and it would be good to clarify whether or not a pilot can use his own Willpower in place of Power ( I would be inclined to say &quot;No&quot; unless the Pilot has a special merit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T13:56:40-07:00","id":621612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=621586#post621586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Real Mecha</b><br /> <br /> Well, Hell. We are living in the future now, aren't we?<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Updates</b><br /> <br /> I replaced the Battery Upgrade with &quot;Generator&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the main stats for the baseline Mechs, we would want to establish what the base recovery time is for Power ( I am thinking 1 power/Hour would be fair). and it would be good to clarify whether or not a pilot can use his own Willpower in place of Power ( I would be inclined to say &quot;No&quot; unless the Pilot has a special merit).</div> </div> </div> </div>I did some changes yeah. So, I guess we're pretty much... done with this homebrew, atleast when it comes to mundane things. I'm wondering what kinds of practical applications Supernaturals would have. I can't see at all werewolves taking mechs since they can easily overpower them already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T13:40:36-07:00","id":624578,"title":"","content":"So I'm working on a supernatural power set that works with mechs direcrly. Pending balancing and revision is the below. Not sure about it, but it's the bare minimum of what I want to do. It's a bit inspired by Eva.<br /> <br /> <br /> Embodied in the Machine<br /> Walkers though they are often built emulating the human form are still no more than fancy vehicles and machines. They retain this property no matter who or what controls them. Atleast that's how things should be. <br /> Some denizens of the dark possess a strange talent that transcends mere controlling or piloting walkers through technopathy. Some learn of a unique talent to directly merge their consciousness with their piloted mech. <br /> Such pilots become able to pilot their mech without the need of even traditional controls, the machine obeys their will perfectly. A mage that is missing both arms and legs doesn't need them to pilot the mech. Certain supernatural powers, dependant on the type of supernatural being, can directly be used on the mech as if the Machine was a true extention of the supernatural's body, such as the werewolf's strength gifts or vampire vigor and celerity.<br /> <br /> Additionally, all attempts to subvert the machine away from the pilots desires or outright destroy it (such as by Unmake) either through supernatural powers or mundane hacking reduce the effectiveness of such attempts by the pilots power stat. If said means are already penalized by the pilots power trait, the power trait applies again.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this synchronization comes with a drawback. Whatever damage the walker takes is also infinite to the pilot. Any structure damage inflicts lethal damage directly on the pilot as through the pilot himself was struck by the attack himself. Any tilts inflicted as a result of damage onto the Walker are also inflicted on the pilot. Including limb loss. The psychic connection creates violent damage feedback onto the pilots body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T12:39:28-07:00","id":633704,"title":"","content":"Just pulled out a massive overhaul of the Original post and a post below it.<br /> <br /> I have successfully updated, consolidted, and fine tuned a few aspects of Mechs.<br /> <br /> Mechs now have a fuel mechanic in the form of fuelcells instead of gasoline simply to future proof it incase Hurt locker comes out. I have modified some conditions to help reflect this change. Power has been modified and more thought out with implications and uses being indicated.<br /> <br /> An entire section devoted to supernatural Mech things has been added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T16:13:53-07:00","id":633920,"title":"","content":"Awesome Update! I will be adding this to my own files [ I have been wanting to run a Space-Opera game using the WoD mechanics for a while, so solid Mech rules fit perfectly.]<br /> Now to make rules for aliens and cyborgs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T20:59:10-07:00","id":634225,"title":"","content":"Well, Deviant should be able to handle Cyborgs. Aliens easily under Infinite Macabre rules. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways got 2 more &quot;special&quot; mechs into the list today.<br /> Amechra submitted this &quot;superrobot&quot; version of the JTAA, which is so uber it needs to maim the user to use it. It's pretty much an &quot;endgame&quot; style option, which is nice. Because sometimes we need to go ove the top<br /> <br /> And I submitted a dragon statue that can be used like a Mech. You can find them in the Front Page under &quot;Gameline Specific Mechs&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T18:24:46-07:00","id":672630,"title":"","content":"I don't think self-repairing machines are so unlikely that you need to claim that they &quot;violate reason&quot;...<br /> There certainly exist many supernatural abilities that fly in the face of the laws of physics and biology (say, a vampire not requiring any functional organs to move a body around) but certainly not this one...such technologies already exist in fact...<br /> Not all repairs require replacement parts anyway (and damage that works by actually destroying physical material rather than just aiming to render machinery inoperational is even rarer).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T19:56:43-07:00","id":672792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=672630#post672630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think self-repairing machines are so unlikely that you need to claim that they &quot;violate reason&quot;...<br /> There certainly exist many supernatural abilities that fly in the face of the laws of physics and biology (say, a vampire not requiring any functional organs to move a body around) but certainly not this one...such technologies already exist in fact...<br /> Not all repairs require replacement parts anyway (and damage that works by actually destroying physical material rather than just aiming to render machinery inoperational is even rarer).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm referring specifically self repair and self maintenance that violates conservation of mass/energy. Note that the upgrade refers to every weapons system being reloaded in addition to self repairs. Self repairs which, though it doesn't outright state it, also technically include replacing any damage due to completely severed off limbs without any need to input replacement parts. <br /> <br /> This is either blatant magic or super science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T21:20:39-07:00","id":672865,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has already been covered, but I just thought I'd share a few ideas on &quot;racial splats&quot; in regards to Mecha...<br /> <br /> Vampires: As a race focused on stealth and subterfuge over flash and violence, vampires don't have much use for mecha. That said, between their political ties and their ancient lineages, it's not uncommon for vampires to have &quot;appropriated&quot; technological mecha, or various forms of relic mecha - golems and the like. They also produce two kinds of mecha of their own; necrocrafts, and blightents.<br /> <br /> Necrocrafts are the most monstrous of all mecha in the world of darkness. These horrific golems are crafted only by bloodlines who have found a way to extend the control of the Blood over dead flesh and bone, necromancer-vampires such as the Burakumin and the Sangiovanni. A necrocraft is a mecha-golem of bones and carrion sewn or magically molded together, and fueled by vitae. Whilst some necrocrafts are fashioned that they anchor themselves into the dead flesh of a vampire &quot;pilot&quot; and use them as simultaneously fuel and pilot, most are designed to respond only to the dark disciplines of their creators, ensuring their monopoly.<br /> <br /> Blightents are the rarest of all mecha. They are an incredibly rare form of mandragora - ghouled plants nourished with vampire blood and shaped into strange, wooden golem-armors. A vampire enters such a construct and is impaled by synchro-thorns, his vitae coursing through the veins of this unliving plant and making them of one mind and body. Although certainly bizarre to look at, blightents are deceptively swift and agile, controlled by the very thoughts of their pilot and translating their every thought into action.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mages: The fashioning of war-golems and battle-armor is one of the lost arts of the mages, and those few who can still do so in the modern nights are a treasured rarity. Each of the Pentacle Orders keeps its magical mecha carefully guarded, and they all have them, although they are stereotypically most numerous amongst the Diamond Arrow and the Free Council. Most Mage mecha are clearly mystical in nature, amazing constructs of Forces and Matter, always highly individualized and treated. Such mecha are hidden away from humans at all costs, for fear of Quiescence unraveling these wondrous relics and reducing them to nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolves: The children of Mother Luna and Father Wolf have the least need for mecha of almost any race, imbued as they are with the blessings of pack and power. Those few that they have are literally Relics - enchanted statues or armor augmented by bound Spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Changelings: Ironically, the hidden folk are the most likely of all the creatures of the night to have mecha at their disposal, by virtue of various dreamspun and hedgewoven constructs. These vary widely, from clearly magical statues of animated elemental matter to bizarre magiteknological constructs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Prometheans: It's rare indeed to see a Promethean controlling a mecha. They are more likely to seek transmutations that let them assimilate flesh and/or metal into themselves, transforming into hulking gargantuas that can <i>match</i> mecha instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters: Mecha created by sin-eaters are typically heaved up from the Underworld, strange Twilight constructs of ghostly machinery liberated from the Dead Dominions. Other sin-eater mecha are &quot;technological golems&quot;; they look like robots, but their powers come from the ghosts that have been convinced or coerced to possess and manipulate the machinery.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mummies: The Arisen occasionally produce mecha in the form of Relics, enchanted armor and golems left over from the days of Irem.<br /> <br /> <br /> Demons: As a demon might be forced to admit, they <b>are</b> basically killer magical robots. What do they need mecha for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T21:44:01-07:00","id":672880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=672865#post672865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has already been covered, but I just thought I'd share a few ideas on &quot;racial splats&quot; in regards to Mecha...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're good. I never really put much thought into racial specific variants. I only made slight, minor upgrades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Vampires: As a race focused on stealth and subterfuge over flash and violence, vampires don't have much use for mecha. That said, between their political ties and their ancient lineages, it's not uncommon for vampires to have &quot;appropriated&quot; technological mecha, or various forms of relic mecha - golems and the like. They also produce two kinds of mecha of their own; necrocrafts, and blightents.<br /> <br /> Necrocrafts are the most monstrous of all mecha in the world of darkness. These horrific golems are crafted only by bloodlines who have found a way to extend the control of the Blood over dead flesh and bone, necromancer-vampires such as the Burakumin and the Sangiovanni. A necrocraft is a mecha-golem of bones and carrion sewn or magically molded together, and fueled by vitae. Whilst some necrocrafts are fashioned that they anchor themselves into the dead flesh of a vampire &quot;pilot&quot; and use them as simultaneously fuel and pilot, most are designed to respond only to the dark disciplines of their creators, ensuring their monopoly.<br /> <br /> Blightents are the rarest of all mecha. They are an incredibly rare form of mandragora - ghouled plants nourished with vampire blood and shaped into strange, wooden golem-armors. A vampire enters such a construct and is impaled by synchro-thorns, his vitae coursing through the veins of this unliving plant and making them of one mind and body. Although certainly bizarre to look at, blightents are deceptively swift and agile, controlled by the very thoughts of their pilot and translating their every thought into action. </div> </div> </div>Quite fascinating. I take it you know Vampire the most given the details.<br /> <br /> I will note Blightents probably should count as Synchronized Mecha given the description. And Necrocrafts would be a slight modification on the Bloodthirsty Upgrade on reply #2 or 3 on the first page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages: The fashioning of war-golems and battle-armor is one of the lost arts of the mages, and those few who can still do so in the modern nights are a treasured rarity. Each of the Pentacle Orders keeps its magical mecha carefully guarded, and they all have them, although they are stereotypically most numerous amongst the Diamond Arrow and the Free Council. Most Mage mecha are clearly mystical in nature, amazing constructs of Forces and Matter, always highly individualized and treated. Such mecha are hidden away from humans at all costs, for fear of Quiescence unraveling these wondrous relics and reducing them to nothing. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you read my mind on this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves: The children of Mother Luna and Father Wolf have the least need for mecha of almost any race, imbued as they are with the blessings of pack and power. Those few that they have are literally Relics - enchanted statues or armor augmented by bound Spirits. </div> </div> </div>Well, there <i>is </i>a need if you consider that some packs need mecha to improve their ranged combat ability. Suppressing fire could be useful in a hunt.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it's a piece of equipment used to allow a Wolfblooded member (of which packs will likely have some in 2e) to keep up with the fully fledged werewolf. I do admit it is rather unlikely for a werewolf pack from using this outside of heavily scifi settings. And besides, some werewolves could literally just tear a mech in half with a single attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Changelings: Ironically, the hidden folk are the most likely of all the creatures of the night to have mecha at their disposal, by virtue of various dreamspun and hedgewoven constructs. These vary widely, from clearly magical statues of animated elemental matter to bizarre magiteknological constructs. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I completely forgot about Hedgespun. Man, they must have some interesting guises outside of the Hedge.<br /> Also,consider the insanity that is a cold iron plated mecha.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prometheans: It's rare indeed to see a Promethean controlling a mecha. They are more likely to seek transmutations that let them assimilate flesh and/or metal into themselves, transforming into hulking gargantuas that can <i>match</i> mecha instead. </div> </div> </div>Well, of course, most mecha are actually fairly unimpressive once Supernaturals move into the mid tier. Most splats with buff centric abilities can outmuscle lights fairly easily. With prometheans though, it's fairly thematic for flesh to overcome steel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sin-Eaters: Mecha created by sin-eaters are typically heaved up from the Underworld, strange Twilight constructs of ghostly machinery liberated from the Dead Dominions. Other sin-eater mecha are &quot;technological golems&quot;; they look like robots, but their powers come from the ghosts that have been convinced or coerced to possess and manipulate the machinery. </div> </div> </div>Don't Sineaters already have a power that explicitly makes them possess machines?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummies: The Arisen occasionally produce mecha in the form of Relics, enchanted armor and golems left over from the days of Irem. </div> </div> </div>I keep having the funny thought that maybe one of the Arisen has a Mecha-TOMB that acts as a mobile shelter and does all of the fighting while he sleeps.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons: As a demon might be forced to admit, they <b>are</b> basically killer magical robots. What do they need mecha for? </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly unprecidented for robots to pilot other robots in fiction. The idea is usually along the veins of more firepower.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm fairly sure that Mecha would technically allow the demon to use Embeds or Exploits through the machines. Perhaps using Mecha might have advantages such as by having external Aether storage or even Aether generators.<br /> <br /> And of course, there's the idea that demons could gut angels to make them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you for the ideas. Some of them I hadn't thought up until you brought up the possibility by mentioning why some splats would have or wouldn't use mecha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T22:42:07-07:00","id":672898,"title":"","content":"Not so much that I know Vampire best as they were the only ones who had such clear and distinctive answers to the question of &quot;so, besides stolen/purchased human tech and ancient relic-mecha, what options does this race have for creating mecha all on their own&quot;?<br /> <br /> I was partly out of my head with the heat when I wrote that post, but I'm glad you found it useful.<br /> <br /> In general summary, my thoughts were that mages and changelings are most likely to have or make mechs, vampires can create necromantic mechs out of mandragora or reanimated corpses, sin-eaters can make mechs out of possessed machinery or from &quot;gear-ghosts&quot; taken from the Underworld, mummies have mech-esque golems and pseudo-power armor relics, and demons/prometheans/werewolves are more likely to have powers that let them transform into states that can counter mecha.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, the Technological Key does let Sin-Eaters possess machinery themselves with certain Manifestations, in addition to commanding ghosts who have possessed statues or machines.<br /> <br /> And I was basically referring to the fact that, in demon form, many demons could probably match or exceed mechs, in addition to generally looking mechanical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T22:49:33-07:00","id":672899,"title":"","content":"Animate + Demon Car =&gt; Lambda. Use a hollow statue as the materials. Animate provides locomotion, turning it into a vehicle, Demon Car passes the Demon's Form abilities to the new &quot;vehicle&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T23:11:00-07:00","id":672942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=672898#post672898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I was basically referring to the fact that, in demon form, many demons could probably match or exceed mechs, in addition to generally looking mechanical.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true for most supernaturals, at least once you get the exp rolling.<br /> <br /> You need quite alot of experiance to outright be superior to a Mecha in every way, some splats do it easier than others. Also, using Demon form itself has its own disadvantages using more &quot;mundane&quot; methods do not have, so that's one advantage Mechs have over using Demon form. Ironically, it's more covert against the God Machine.<br /> <br /> Mechs as written by this project lean heavily towards the early or mid game for supernaturals. This is most likely the result of trying to keep Mecha as &quot;Real robot&quot; as possible, not <i>too </i>overpowering, but powerful enough. Mid-late game supernaturals of all stride dominate them, but this point requires quite a bit of experiance. I mean, how much experiance does it take to beat a Tactical or Heavy laser in terms of weapon damage and absurd AP with given range values?<br /> <br /> The secondary purpose of Mechs though, at least once we're at the superhuman point where other players can have base attributes of 6+ or be werewolves and <i>grapple </i>with Mecha right at the start of the game, is that allows a mortal player to still be relatively relevant in such a high powered part. Especially once you start cracking out the supernatural upgrades to say, make the Mecha hard to just subvert and deck it with weaponry that could mission kill tanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, anyone consider Beast mechs? They'd be the even more unlikely users themselves, admittedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:07:02-08:00","id":760248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3436-conspiracy-the-brotherhood-prizrakov\">Let's add some special materials, shall we?</a><br /> <br /> <b>Contracting and Mechs:</b> Trying to use a Soulsteel mech without the benefits of the Brotherhood's contract is... ill-advised. In addition to the normal problems with using a tool uncontracted, you also suffer 1L whenever a point of Fuel is spent.<br /> <br /> <b>Stygium:</b> A mech made of Stygium grants the pilot the benefits of a Stygium Icon; however, the pilot must spend Fuel instead of Willpower, allowing the sensors to &quot;sniff out&quot; any nearby Ghosts in Twilight.<br /> <b>Khimertut:</b> A pilot contracted to a mech made of Khimertut improves the Handling by two, In addition, they may spend one Fuel as an Instant action to remove one Tilt the mech is suffering from, psychoreactive metal reforming to compensate for lost struts and broken wiring.<br /> <b>Krovstal:</b> A Krovstal mech readily drinks in the blood of its pilot - the pilot may choose to reflexively take 1L to have the mech regain one point of Fuel.<br /> <b>Zexonyte:</b> A mech incorporating Zexonyte parts gains +2/+0 Armor against magic, as defined by Zexonyte armor.<br /> <b>Bleshkota:</b> A mech with Bleshkota plating increases its Durability by one against unarmed attacks.<br /> <b>P-Lichina:</b> A mech incorporating P-Lichina serves as a P-Lichina Icon. Much like Stygium, however, the pilot spends Fuel instead of Willpower.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T10:42:04-08:00","id":760750,"title":"","content":"Very nice. Wasn't expecting this to be posted in yesterday.<br /> <br /> I do kinda wonder how expensive it would be to totally coat a giant robot in exotic metals. Then again that conspiracy does strike me as having an enormously large budget.<br /> <br /> Although it's probably a funny thing to see a superheated out preform a lighter tier model because of Khimertut used on every valid piece.<br /> <br /> Hm, I wonder what kind of Frankensteining TCG would apply to mechs....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T08:24:12-08:00","id":765569,"title":"","content":"I see this and I can't help thinking of CthulhuTech.. not a bad thing .. I liked CthulhuTech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T13:28:20-08:00","id":765758,"title":"","content":"I only skimmed your updated OP so maybe I missed it, but I didn't actually see anything about how Defense is determined when piloting these mechs. Seems kinda important, especially when you have made them as offensively powerful as you have. Those high Strength scores will massively bias mech melee towards endurance battles cause of the near impossibility of missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T15:15:48-08:00","id":765830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthMRN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=765758#post765758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only skimmed your updated OP so maybe I missed it, but I didn't actually see anything about how Defense is determined when piloting these mechs. Seems kinda important, especially when you have made them as offensively powerful as you have. Those high Strength scores will massively bias mech melee towards endurance battles cause of the near impossibility of missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Within the big spoiler text under &quot;Mech rules&quot;, paragraph 5:<br /> &quot;Due to their legged nature allowing for quick deviations of motion, Mechs possess a Defense score. Defense is calculated as the lower of the pilot\u2019s Dexterity or Wits (Or Finesse in the case of nonphysical drivers) + Drive (or Pilot if you prefer). Defense is penalized by the Mech\u2019s Handling due to the size and bulk of the walker, but bonuses to Handling do not raise Defense. Obviously, an unpiloted Mech is considered as having a Defense of 0.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing about Mech Melee is that they have good durability ratings to reduce damage. In, that's a rule of Mech combat in general. You're more mobile than most other vehicles, but you're not relying on evasion all of the time; your armor takes hits for you when you can't dodge.<br /> <br /> You did remind me that Mech melee should be able to hurt other mechs though, so now every Mech has AP ratings to go along with its melee weapons. So thanks for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T15:16:43-08:00","id":765831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=765569#post765569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this and I can't help thinking of CthulhuTech.. not a bad thing .. I liked CthulhuTech.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I haven't made any eldritch alien invader mechs yet... but it's on my list of fun things to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T16:32:12-08:00","id":765866,"title":"","content":"With two out of three mech types having pretty hefty Handling penalties, that looks like in most cases it will be a quite low Defense score compared to being on foot (since it appears the Handling booster merit doesn't add to it). Versus a pretty high attack pool due to Strength. Now, if as you say, this is intentional, cause they are meant to be tanking those inevitable hits, that would be fair enough. But with melee AP on top, that really eyeballs as a very offensively biased system. One that will end fights after a handful of hits even without good rolls. Not what I would call in line with GMC.<br /> <br /> Which bodes ill for the ranged system, with its insanely high damage ratings and AP values. Remember that AP effectively neutralizes Durability, in which case you are back to normal human combat + whatever increase you have made to the GMC weapon ratings, in this case a lot. A doubling of the &quot;Health&quot; track won't do much to hold that back. One of those Damage 5 mid-range guns of yours will remove Durability from the equation easily, after which even a 23 Structure Heavy Mech won't hold out for more than a few turns. And at that scale, cover is harder to come by to compensate for no Defense application. To say nothing of more powerful guns and lighter mechs.<br /> <br /> Pure experienced eyeballing here, but this system currently seems as deadly as GMC, but because of mechs inevitably getting scrapped fast due to offensive bias, rather than lucky dice rolls. Have you done any playtesting? Seems like the easiest way to get a feel for where adjustments are needed to maintain the fun factor of using tech like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T17:18:05-08:00","id":765893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthMRN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=765866#post765866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With two out of three mech types having pretty hefty Handling penalties, that looks like in most cases it will be a quite low Defense score compared to being on foot (since it appears the Handling booster merit doesn't add to it). Versus a pretty high attack pool due to Strength. Now, if as you say, this is intentional, cause they are meant to be tanking those inevitable hits, that would be fair enough. But with melee AP on top, that really eyeballs as a very offensively biased system. One that will end fights after a handful of hits even without good rolls. Not what I would call in line with GMC.<br /> <br /> Which bodes ill for the ranged system, with its insanely high damage ratings and AP values. Remember that AP effectively neutralizes Durability, in which case you are back to normal human combat + whatever increase you have made to the GMC weapon ratings, in this case a lot. A doubling of the &quot;Health&quot; track won't do much to hold that back. One of those Damage 5 mid-range guns of yours will remove Durability from the equation easily, after which even a 23 Structure Heavy Mech won't hold out for more than a few turns. And at that scale, cover is harder to come by to compensate for no Defense application. To say nothing of more powerful guns and lighter mechs.<br /> <br /> Pure experienced eyeballing here, but this system currently seems as deadly as GMC, but because of mechs inevitably getting scrapped fast due to offensive bias, rather than lucky dice rolls. Have you done any playtesting? Seems like the easiest way to get a feel for where adjustments are needed to maintain the fun factor of using tech like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many of the really big guns are by design hilariously over the top to be effective against vehicles as some of them supposed to be antitank. And walkers which are considerably less damage resistant than tanks are gonna get croaked easily. The AP and damage values are gonna change if I get a good sampling of Armored vehicles to compare to post GMC, but for now, I have to design those guns to work against Heavy tanks from 1e. I suppose the primary thing to do to discourage them from being used against foot troops via some sort of &quot;lock on&quot; requirements as well as tone down the ridiculous AP on some of them to be more in line with fighting other mechs. This a good idea?<br /> <br /> As for melee, what do you recommend? You're the first one to specifically bring this issue to me and while I have done some testing, I haven't yet actually had the opportunity to. use them in actual play. Should I buff the Durabilities, cut down the APs just slightly? I could also drop Handling penalties and instead replace them with specific defense penalties. You're the one with the experiance, I will listen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T07:03:03-08:00","id":766222,"title":"","content":"It makes sense to me to use the 1e Main Battle Tank as a basis. But without knowing what you intend for mechs, I'm not sure what changes to recommend. If they are supposed to be at once capable of taking down such a tank in a few hits, but be no more durable themselves, you seem to be spot on, however dangerous and undesirable that will make mech battles. But if they are supposed to be superior in some fashion, while treating tanks as fodder, something extra is needed. Maybe boosing Defense, or simply Durability.<br /> <br /> Melee seems to be less of a problem than ranged, so I'm not too sure here. A good guideline is to pit two equal versions of the weakest minimum mech against each other, and then two maxed out versions as well, and see how these play out. Two unmerited civ mechs with average pilots seems reasonable, where the lack of AP will give Durability 3 plenty of protection even against high Strength scores, leading to the sort of endurance brawls you mentioned. But I'm more worried about the maxed out heavy mechs piloted by aces, cause I got the impression there are more offensive merits than defensive ones, which means easy to hit melee attacks with large AP and Damage bonuses, counteracted by minimal Defense and only moderate AP armour. I get the feeling you will be disappointed by how well these monsters hold up against attacks from their peers.<br /> <br /> The most specific I can be is to look at what GMC did with Defense: Two equal opponents nullify each others' attacks on average dice rolls, with only Willpower and luck being able to break the tie. If you can acheve a stat-wise equilibrium where the same goes for mech melee, without taking away their ability to treat tanks as fodder on the side, you will be where I think you want to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T07:50:15-08:00","id":766251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthMRN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=766222#post766222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense to me to use the 1e Main Battle Tank as a basis. But without knowing what you intend for mechs, I'm not sure what changes to recommend. If they are supposed to be at once capable of taking down such a tank in a few hits, but be no more durable themselves, you seem to be spot on, however dangerous and undesirable that will make mech battles. But if they are supposed to be superior in some fashion, while treating tanks as fodder, something extra is needed. Maybe boosing Defense, or simply Durability.<br /> <br /> Melee seems to be less of a problem than ranged, so I'm not too sure here. A good guideline is to pit two equal versions of the weakest minimum mech against each other, and then two maxed out versions as well, and see how these play out. Two unmerited civ mechs with average pilots seems reasonable, where the lack of AP will give Durability 3 plenty of protection even against high Strength scores, leading to the sort of endurance brawls you mentioned. But I'm more worried about the maxed out heavy mechs piloted by aces, cause I got the impression there are more offensive merits than defensive ones, which means easy to hit melee attacks with large AP and Damage bonuses, counteracted by minimal Defense and only moderate AP armour. I get the feeling you will be disappointed by how well these monsters hold up against attacks from their peers.<br /> <br /> The most specific I can be is to look at what GMC did with Defense: Two equal opponents nullify each others' attacks on average dice rolls, with only Willpower and luck being able to break the tie. If you can acheve a stat-wise equilibrium where the same goes for mech melee, without taking away their ability to treat tanks as fodder on the side, you will be where I think you want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They aren't MBT level, no. If they were, they'd be size 20 and have Durabilities above 10. The specific intention of Mechs was a transition unit between powered armor and armored cars capable of engaging foes ranging from infantry all the way up to vehicle warfare. Their primary advantage over other vehicles is supposed to be their mobility, their ability to engage at melee, and unlike infantry can carry weapons normally too large for humans on their own. It's like, trying to combine the advantages of infantry and applying them to a vehicle. I admittedly may have over nerfed the defense rating with such really high Handling penalties.<br /> <br /> Sadly, it's not exactly easy to balance ranged combat. But to be fair, this is the situation you kind of face when you mount antitank weaponry to light to medium vehicles, which Mechs fit into. It's worth noting though that some of the really powerful weapons are considered &quot;Strength M&quot;, which means the Mech has to be a Superheavy to use them without penalty. Heavies get a -3 Penalty and Lights and Civies get a -8 so that'll cut down on them being used improperly.<br /> <br /> I did buff super heavies just now upping their health and durability, as well as reduce Handling penalties on all levels. This should mean that Defense factors in more.<br /> Also, there's an option to Boost your mechs to apply Defense against Firearms. Really important upgrade that I think reduces the effectiveness at ranged combat, especially against foes using oversized weapons.<br /> <br /> As of now, after some adjustments to the stats, a ranged fight between Superheavies is now a bit more of a slugfest. Weapons barring the Autocannons and Lasers now don't do so much damage relative to Superheavies which have Durability 11. Most other weapons are going to need either more successess to damage them or do somewhere around 10% of the Mech's total health, which I think is fitting as Superheavies are meant to be tanky. Dedicated antitank weapons on a successful hit will do somewhere around a third of a Superheavy's health. This is not even factoring upgrades, which will make it more offense or defense oriented ( a subsystem you might have missed out on on the first pass). Notable upgrades include penalizing firearms attacks, reducing the effectiveness of armor piercing, mobility options like flight. And so on.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T14:05:48-08:00","id":766519,"title":"","content":"I take Mech \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 to get a Super-Heavy Mech. Then I put three dots each in Armor Enhancement, Enhanced Safety Features, Handling Enhancement, and Hardened Armor.<br /> <br /> My mech has literally every point of general defensive enhancement they can get their hands on. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Class</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Strength</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Durability</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Size</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Structure</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Acceleration</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Safe Speed</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Max Speed</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Handling</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Power</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Tank McGee</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">13</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">14</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">18</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">32</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">20</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">+0</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">2</td> </tr> </table></div> It also ignores 3 points of AP, and blocks three points of damage that would be dealt to the pilot.<br /> <br /> Let's look at what would happen if I bought a different Super-Heavy Mech, and put three dots in Strength Enhancement, four dots in Melee Modification, two in Handling Enhancement, and three in Neural Interface. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Class</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Strength</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Durability</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Size</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Structure</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Acceleration</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Safe Speed</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Max Speed</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Handling</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Power</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">Punchman 24000</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">16</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">11</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">18</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">29</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">20</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">-1</td> <td class=\"text_table_text_table_td\">2</td> </tr> </table></div> It also has AP 7 on +9L fists, and the pilot uses the higher of their Wits and Dexterity for Defense.<br /> <br /> Punchman 24000 would have to get at least 2 successes to deal even one damage to Tanks McGee; Tanks McGee, on the other hand, can't even scratch Punchman 24000 without getting at least 4 successes on their roll. Tank McGee can't even <i>hurt</i> another Tank McGee without getting <i>ten successes.</i> Punchman 24000 could hurt another Punchman 24000 normally, their massive fists dealing at 6L+ each time they land.<br /> <br /> For comparison, Punchman 24000's fists have a higher damage rating than any of the mech weapons you can use, and have a higher AP rating than any of the weapons other than the lasers and the Autocannons (at least, the ones that aren't the High-Speed Autocannon - that thing doesn't have any AP!)<br /> <br /> So I load a Heavy Autocannon on Punchman 24000. Now I can just rip through Tank McGee with little to no problem. And if he brings his friend Speedy McMech to the party, who's in a Light Mech with all <i>kinds</i> of Boost... I just punch it. Because I'll be dealing 10L+ a punch, and my attack will take the same penalty either way.<br /> <br /> Make of this what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T14:08:58-08:00","id":766523,"title":"","content":"Oh, and a question - how does Heavy Recoil work with stuff that are Strength M?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T16:46:10-08:00","id":766647,"title":"","content":"Alright, so, going all in on Defense isn't as powerful as going all in on offense as defensive tanking isn't really... worth it as you can't get good enough melee to deal damage to other mechs. That actually kinda makes a bit of sense and I think I'm kinda okay with that.<br /> <br /> Punchman should honestly be able to rip appart lighter Mechs with ease. Granted, a Light Mech should have a mobility advantage to allow him to say snipe off Punchman, it's kinda how I feel that that sort of scenario should play out. So, that part is satisfactory.<br /> <br /> On the otherhand, mechs should be atleast be able to do glancing damage to each other or rip appart each other's limbs. I mean, it should be possible for a Tanky mech to atleast slowly grind away at a more offensively stronger mech.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, perhaps means to go after the pilot are neccesary? Some sort of Grappling fight? Or maybe the ability to make called Shots to limbs to mission kill a Mech? On the otherhand, Tank doesn't have nearly enough melee offense to counter Punchy using those tools against him. On the other hand, I kinda feel that is working as intended as Tank has invested in defense, but no offense to counter an offense oriented bot where as Punchy has offense. Yet Punchy is too tough for Tank to fight, the disparity in ability is just that great. That part vexes me.<br /> <br /> Well, my considerations right now are to buff melee some more, so that atleast Tank can hurt Punchy, even though it also buffs Punchy. I slightly nerfed the Melee modification so atleast Punchy and Tanky need the same ammount of successes to hurt each other. If I buffed &quot;standard&quot; Melee ability for Heavies and thus by proxy superheavies, that means Punchy and Tanky need the same ammount of damage to each other even then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Size M, I added text basically stating they count as having Strength 10+ for Heavy Recoil's purposes. + because autofire increases it. Atleast for now, might drop it lower for later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 11-15-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:58:18-08:00","id":767398,"title":"","content":"If these mechs are intended to be Ellen Ripley in Aliens, except with enormous mobility, that is beyond my range of experience. But I like how you have taken the maxed out versions and pitted them against each other. Seems like you have discovered a lot of how they work out mechanically vs the ideal you had in mind already. Keep doing that and you'll have this sorted to satisfaction soon enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T00:54:00-08:00","id":771309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthMRN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=767398#post767398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If these mechs are intended to be Ellen Ripley in Aliens, except with enormous mobility, that is beyond my range of experience. But I like how you have taken the maxed out versions and pitted them against each other. Seems like you have discovered a lot of how they work out mechanically vs the ideal you had in mind already. Keep doing that and you'll have this sorted to satisfaction soon enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth mentioning that that's the reason we have a Civilian Mech in the first place. If you pay very close attention, it basically simulates the very basic Mech she used in the finale of Aliens. Right down to the fact it leaves the user very exposed and isn't a full body seal.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I've made a minor sorting on just now. All Mechs now have enough Base weapon damage and ap to at the very minimum damage other mechs of the same type barring upgrades <br /> <br /> As a consequence of this.... mech melee is brutally effective on anything smaller than it. Civilian Mechs have 3 damage, light is the same but adds AP 2. And heavies deal 5 with AP 3...<br /> <br /> As you can see, they'll rip appart human level opponents and smaller mechs easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:31:54-08:00","id":824992,"title":"","content":"So, with the recent reveal of &quot;dramatic reloads&quot; existing to basically remove reloading except for in specific cirvumatances, I wonder how I should adjust them when converting said rules.... but for combat robots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just as well, I'm wondering about tweaking some things in this project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:25:22-08:00","id":833993,"title":"","content":"Alright ladies and gentlemen, Mere moments after just getting the new Cod Book, I have finally updated Mechs to account Hurt Locker Appendix Preview and the new Corebook rules to the best of my ability.<br /> <br /> I have changed over all Mechs to have a single speed and in the process massively increased most speeds to account for this. I have made it so the Light Mech no longer gets the insane jump boosters as previously, but the thing runs almost as fast as a car now. and the Heavy Mech is really fast for its size.<br /> <br /> The Boost upgrade now instantly accelerates a mech to its top speed.<br /> <br /> Also, now all guns reflect the Hurt Locker specific gun ranges and ammo capacities. Most guns are really high range but then again, said weapons are obscenely powerful due to their size.<br /> <br /> Long story short, mechs are faster than you'd think and you should reall","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 02-20-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T19:48:38-08:00","id":834199,"title":"","content":"Nice.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm thinking of adding my own contributions to the project after the Mage 2E book and the Huntsmen's weapons are spoiled.<br /> <br /> Namely, an Artifact mech sent by the Exarchs to serve as the steed of a tetrarch's most trusted bodyguard, and a Huntsman's harness that unfolds into the perfect power armor for subduing and stalking their quarry. The <i>Peleps</i> and the Herne's Mantle, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T19:50:13-08:00","id":834200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=834199#post834199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm thinking of adding my own contributions to the project after the Mage 2E book and the Huntsmen's weapons are spoiled.<br /> <br /> Namely, an Artifact mech sent by the Exarchs to serve as the steed of a tetrarch's most trusted bodyguard, and a Huntsman's harness that unfolds into the perfect power armor for subduing and stalking their quarry. The <i>Peleps</i> and the Herne's Mantle, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sweet. You're welcome to do so at any time. Though I'm wondering if it's really neccesary to wait for them to be released. Is there anything specific you need from them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:02:31-08:00","id":834209,"title":"","content":"Just the Artifact and Arcadian Weapons mechanics, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T13:04:17-08:00","id":834591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=834209#post834209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just the Artifact and Arcadian Weapons mechanics, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dunno. A part of me wonders if such rules would be sufficient. I suppose you can improvise something later though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, you just reminded me something I wanted to make:<br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WereMech(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Special) </span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Wolf-Blooded</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effects:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Many Wolf-Blooded dream of the day that they might one day join the pack in </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Siskur</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">-</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Dah</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">, not as a mere helper, but part of the center stage. Above all else, they fantasize about the power the Killing Form, doing more than simply harrying it so that others might earn the glory. With the advent of bipedal walkers, clever Wolfblooded found an alternative outlet. Through a combination of spirit magic and neurotransmitters, they can see the world through a werewolf\u2019s perspective.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The --- is a converted Civilian grade Mech, usually previous a power loader or construction unit. The changes often involve putting metal or wooden masks or carving heads to resemble a wolf\u2019s. Other typical accessories include animal pelts sown together like a cape, upscaled weapons for use in combat, and scripture in the First Tongue.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">But one thing that is common in all --- is the binding of a powerful Wolf spirit to the body, granting the machine a small measure of the power that belonging to a true Uratha. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The --- is a Civilian Mech with the following changes to the base form:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 Strength, +2 Durability, +2 Structure, +2 Handling, -5 Energy</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sense Link:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While riding in this gigantic Fetish, a Wolf-Blood perceives the world through the senses of the ---. This doesn\u2019t quite work like Synchronization, but it\u2019s close. An operator may use Brawl, Weaponry, and Athletics, where appropriate instead of relying on Drive.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gauru Effigy:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The --- receives the Primal Fear, Perception, and Lunacy special rules as described for Gauru form. Being made to emulate Gauru form, the --- is very proficent at it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bloodlust:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Thrill of the Hunt fuels the very life force of machine, allowing it to function even when it shouldn\u2019t. The --- recovers Structure at a rate of 1 per turn, but only when fighting. This healing does not remove Tilts or Conditions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The --- may take Mech upgrade merits as normal.<br /> <br /> Probably too OP</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 02-21-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T11:18:45-07:00","id":965758,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Old Blood (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b></span><br /> <i>&quot;Handwritten scrawl: Seek paleblood to transcend the hunt.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> A recipient of the Old Blood arises from the operation as something more than human.<br /> <br /> Treat them as if they were wearing a Mech with the following stats:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Class</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Strength</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Durability</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Size</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Structure</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Speed</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Handling</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Power</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Super-Light</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">[Their Strength]</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">[Their Size]</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">[Their Speed]</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">+0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">[Their Stamina]</td> </tr> </table></div> They cannot upgrade this &quot;mech&quot; with the Craft skill and it is permanently subject to the Cockpit Breached Tilt (and don't get the benefits of the Concealment) - in exchange, they have the Going by Feel \u2022, Manual Dexterity \u2022\u2022, Mechanized Combat Training \u2022, and Self-Servicing \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 merits for the purposes of this &quot;mech&quot; only.<br /> <br /> They may purchase Upgrade merits for the &quot;mech&quot; as normal, can wield mech-scale weaponry, and treat time spent sleeping or meditating as being &quot;plugged in&quot; for the purposes of regaining Power. They cannot, however, remove the Cockpit Breached Tilt through any means.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> This is <i>obviously</i> only balanced in a game where mechs are something everyone has access to. With some refluffing, you have something pretty metal - oh, and you <i>can</i> use driving style merits with the Old Blood. Yeah, you're subject to the upgrade cap (that's something new), but that's not <i>too</i> bad.<br /> <br /> (Oh, and Almarck? You might want to update the Speed Enhancement merit - it still references acceleration, safe speed, and maximum speed. You might also want to do that with the Conditions and Tilts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:17:17-07:00","id":965827,"title":"","content":"Good work as always Amechra. Done as requested and added to the first page. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking on it given the sheer modifications involved to make someone essentially a cyborg, that merit is probably something akin to a minor template in terms of effects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:52:05-07:00","id":966569,"title":"","content":"I'm keeping an eye on this for Deviant, because there's really a lot of overlap between giant robots and Deviants. Evangelion, for example, has the perfect atmosphere and tone for a Deviant story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:01:34-07:00","id":966614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=966569#post966569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm keeping an eye on this for Deviant, because there's really a lot of overlap between giant robots and Deviants. Evangelion, for example, has the perfect atmosphere and tone for a Deviant story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... I'll admit, that's not something I ever thought I'd hear anyone say when I made this little project back a year ago. How do you figure that'll work out? Because right now, I can only imagine atleast one Deviant or Rebel will pilot a mech as a heavy ordinance thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:04:30-07:00","id":966617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=966614#post966614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ... I'll admit, that's not something I ever thought I'd hear anyone say when I made this little project back a year ago. How do you figure that'll work out? Because right now, I can only imagine atleast one Deviant or Rebel will pilot a mech as a heavy ordinance thing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Evangelion connection would be to make it so that only certain people, perhaps people who have been genetically altered, can pilot a certain type of mech. Maybe the mech even uses them as a sort of &quot;power source&quot;. <br /> <br /> On a smaller scale, I'm plannin on homebrewing &quot;stabilizers&quot; that let a Deviant use limited amounts of Blowout-level power, and Powered Armor is one of the forms they could take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:05:44-07:00","id":966618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=966617#post966617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the Evangelion connection would be to make it so that only certain people, perhaps people who have been genetically altered, can pilot a certain type of mech. Maybe the mech even uses them as a sort of &quot;power source&quot;.<br /> <br /> On a smaller scale, I'm plannin on homebrewing &quot;stabilizers&quot; that let a Deviant use limited amounts of Blowout-level power, and Powered Armor is one of the forms they could take.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haven't paid attention to Deviant yet. I'm guessing the early powers set is up? I don't understand Blowout since I haven't been in the thread in ages.<br /> <br /> I've actually done quite a bit of work making generic &quot;item&quot; powered armor. Most of my Homebrew seems to revolve around &quot;vanilla&quot; items, usually scifi items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:16:08-07:00","id":966623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=966618#post966618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Haven't paid attention to Deviant yet. I'm guessing the early powers set is up? I don't understand Blowout since I haven't been in the thread in ages.<br /> <br /> I've actually done quite a bit of work making generic &amp;quot;item&amp;quot; powered armor. Most of my Homebrew seems to revolve around &amp;quot;vanilla&amp;quot; items, usually scifi items.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see that, it sounds interesting. And you should check out Deviant. You like scifi stuff, so it's right up your alley. <br /> <br /> The Lemurian Heresy Machine cult that I came up with probably has a few mechs lying around or in garages somewhere. Since they're inspired by the Society of Ether, the Lemurians, and W40K's Imperium, it makes sense that they'd at least try to build them. Their theology basically runs on &quot;what would be cool&quot;, so of course they have giant robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:19:43-07:00","id":966624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect?p=966623#post966623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to see that, it sounds interesting. And you should check out Deviant. You like scifi stuff, so it's right up your alley.<br /> <br /> The Lemurian Heresy Machine cult that I came up with probably has a few mechs lying around or in garages somewhere. Since they're inspired by the Society of Ether, the Lemurians, and W40K's Imperium, it makes sense that they'd at least try to build them. Their theology basically runs on &quot;what would be cool&quot;, so of course they have giant robots.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/859045-conspiracy-guardians-haans-chowdhury-productions-power-armored-and-mech-using-hunters\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-using-hunters</a><br /> <br /> Created a Conspiracy for a currently dormant Fangame involving aliens... I need to update my sig real bad.<br /> <br /> Just keep in mine that the Mechs in this project aren't really all that big. Not even the Superheavy. In terms of mass, it's about an Abrams or less. This was a concession made to have them playable and combatable on foot. <br /> <br /> Once you get past 15 meters, things get crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\"